<div class="analysis-source"><div><strong id="analysis-checkpoint">No checkpoint yet</strong><small id="analysis-source-date"></small></div><button class="button quiet" id="export-analysis">↓ Export analysis JSON</button></div>
<details class="analysis-method"><summary>How to read this table</summary><p><strong>Before / after</strong> are intervals between document text-input events, measured around the inputs that created the first and last surviving letters. Spaces and punctuation count as inputs. Intervals may include time spent in the sidebar or another window. Missing boundaries, unrecorded text, and transferred words show — rather than an invented pause.</p><p><strong>History:</strong> T = typed, I = inserted into an existing word, D = deleted, R = replaced, P = external paste, C = matched internal copy, M = matched internal cut-and-paste, B = bulk input. @ is the source character offset (zero-based). Expand a row for each individual operation and its timestamp. Shared ancestry after word splits, joins, or passage replacement is flagged. Copy/move links are inferred from the last recorded selection and matching pasted text in this document; cross-document and external pastes have no known source.</p><p><strong>Purity</strong> is a heuristic: 100 ÷ (1 + revision operations + transfer/bulk penalty + shared-lineage penalty), rounded. Straightforward typing scores 100. Incomplete ancestry is unknown, never 100. It measures editing history, not quality. Pauses use text inputs rather than keydown events, so mobile input and punctuation follow the same rule.</p></details>
<div id="analysis-warning" role="status"></div><div class="process-stats" id="analysis-stats"></div>
<div class="analysis-display-toolbar"><div class="analysis-display-toggle" role="group" aria-label="Word analysis display"><button type="button" id="analysis-show-heatmap" class="active" aria-pressed="true" aria-controls="analysis-heatmap-panel">Heatmap</button><button type="button" id="analysis-show-table" aria-pressed="false" aria-controls="analysis-table-panel">Table</button></div><p>Latest checkpoint · Tap a word to inspect its history</p></div>
<div id="analysis-heatmap-panel"><div class="heatmap-legend" aria-label="Heatmap color scale"><span><i class="heat-untouched"></i>Typed once</span><span><i class="heat-light"></i>Lightly edited</span><span><i class="heat-moderate"></i>More edited</span><span><i class="heat-heavy"></i>Heavily edited</span><span><i class="heat-unknown"></i>Unknown history</span></div><div id="word-heatmap" class="word-heatmap" aria-label="Checkpoint text with editing heatmap"></div><p class="heatmap-explanation">Color follows purity: green is 100; yellow and orange indicate more revision, transfer, or shared ancestry. Gray hatching means the history is incomplete.</p><section id="heatmap-word-detail" class="heatmap-word-detail" aria-label="Selected word history" aria-live="polite"><p>Select a word to see how it changed.</p></section></div>
