<details class="analysis-method"><summary>Score notation and timing</summary><p><code>&lt;2.329&gt;</code> advances time by 2.329 seconds. <code>&lt;DEL3&gt;</code> backspaces three UTF-16 units; <code>&lt;DEL&gt;</code> backspaces one. <code>&lt;CLICK31&gt;</code> moves to zero-based offset 31. <code>&lt;ENTER&gt;</code> inserts a newline. A delete with a selection removes that selection. Clicks and selections outside the document are rejected.</p><p>Faithful notation is the default. Keyboard moves appear as LEFT, RIGHT, UP, DOWN, HOME, END, or modified keys, with recorded target ranges after @. CLICK and TAP indicate recorded pointer actions. MOVE and SELECT mark recorded positions whose cause is unknown in older logs. Click Make portable for simpler renderers; this may add positioning clicks and change action provenance.</p><p>Optional extensions: <code>&lt;SELECT2:8&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;COPY&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;CUT&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;PASTE&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;FWD&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;TAB&gt;</code>, and <code>&lt;LT&gt;</code> / <code>&lt;GT&gt;</code> for literal angle brackets. Encoded PATCH and BASE tokens preserve bulk edits and snapshots. Unsupported tokens stay in the log with a warning.</p><p>Plain typing runs have no individual letter timings: their letters share the run timestamp, and word analysis marks intra-run intervals as unknown. Generated scores provide a delay for each letter. These are synthetic sessions, not measurements of real typing. A fixed seed and target give the same score. The lossless RICH extension preserves an entire document; importing it forks the document and remaps IDs.</p></details></section>
